# Test: IS-IS doctor checks (spec-isis-13 config-sanity + surfaced raw-socket).
#
# VALIDATES: spec-isis-13 -- the IS-IS doctor codes are registered and explainable
#            (ze explain), and `ze doctor --json` against a config whose explicit
#            system-id disagrees with the NET emits doctor-isis-system-id-mismatch
#            (AC-12). The raw-socket code (owned by isis-3) is surfaced by
#            ze explain too (AC-11 surface); its firing path needs CAP_NET_RAW and
#            is a QEMU integration test, not a .ci.
# PREVENTS:  regression where a config-sanity code is unregistered (not
#            explainable) or the config-sanity check never fires on a bad config.
#
# The net-missing firing path and the raw-socket firing path are covered by the
# doctor unit tests (internal/plugins/isis/doctor_test.go) and isis-3's
# transport doctor test; here we assert the user-visible explain surface for all
# three codes plus the system-id-mismatch doctor run (which parses cleanly
# because the config carries a valid NET).

# The config carries a valid NET (so config verification passes) but an explicit
# system-id that disagrees with the System ID embedded in that NET.
tmpfs=isis-mismatch.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
isis {
	net 49.0001.0000.0000.0001.00
	system-id 0000.0000.0002
	level l1-l2
}
EOF_CONF

# --- All three IS-IS doctor codes are explainable. ---------------------------
# A generous timeout: the runner treats each foreground `ze` as a daemon and,
# with a tmpfs present, waits ~5s per command for a readiness file the one-shot
# `ze explain` / `ze doctor` never writes; four commands need >15s of budget.
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze explain doctor-isis-net-missing:timeout=60s:exit=0
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=doctor-isis-net-missing
expect=stdout:contains=net

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze explain doctor-isis-system-id-mismatch:exit=0
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=doctor-isis-system-id-mismatch
expect=stdout:contains=System ID

cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze explain doctor-isis-raw-socket:exit=0
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=doctor-isis-raw-socket
expect=stdout:contains=CAP_NET_RAW

# --- ze doctor --json fires the system-id-mismatch check (AC-12). ------------
# `ze doctor` exits non-zero when it finds a problem (a SeverityError diagnostic),
# so a fired config-sanity check returns exit code 1 (cf. doctor-config-reference).
cmd=foreground:seq=4:exec=ze doctor --json isis-mismatch.conf:exit=1
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=doctor-isis-system-id-mismatch
